    { "Delete ALL dogs (whole save)", "106cff83", 24 },
    { "Delete EVERY dog in the whole save: all owners, strays included, loaded or not, plus kennel and vehicle records? The far-away part runs in the background; save the game when it reports done. Use this before removing the mod from a save. This cannot be undone.", "13928715", 24 },
    { "Deletes every dog in the save: the loaded ones right away, then sweeps the animal cells on disk for the ones far from any player. Save the game when it reports done.", "fd3f8310", 24 },
    { "Depth: ?", "f6649770", 24 },
    { "Dog thinking interval (ticks)", "7013a44d", 24 },
    { "Empty checks before resting", "6d0624ef", 24 },
    { "Empty zombie checks before a dog starts checking less often. Lower = rests sooner, lighter server. Higher = stays alert longer, more server load.", "e5898f6b", 24 },
    { "Follow stream interval (ms)", "6ba021db", 24 },
    { "Follow update interval (ticks)", "60f952d4", 24 },
    { "Force pregnancy (nearest dog)", "61843db5", 24 },
    { "Forget unreachable zombies (game minutes)", "5af31c77", 24 },
    { "Growth diag", "f217add5", 24 },
    { "Health status", "bdcc8121", 24 },
    { "How far a dog looks for zombies to attack. Lower = only fights up close, lighter server. Higher = engages sooner, more server load.", "509bf687", 24 },
    { "How far a dog moves before recalculating where it can walk. Lower = more accurate, more server load. Higher = lighter server, may get stuck longer. 0 = every step.", "719d5c7b", 24 },
    { "How fast the server looks for places to spawn stray dogs. Lower = lighter server, strays may be lost when busy. Higher = more strays, more server load. Raise only if spawn.qfull stays above zero.", "b6714f02", 24 },
    { "How long a dog remembers where it can walk. Lower = more accurate, more server load. Higher = lighter server, may hold old info. Raise together with the radius below.", "38ffcad7", 24 },
    { "How often a following dog corrects its path. Lower = smoother follow, more server load. Higher = laggy follow, lighter server. Counted in server ticks: on a full server running under 5 ticks a second, 8 here is almost 2 seconds.", "18402665", 24 },
    { "How often dogs forget zombies they could not reach. Lower = tries them again sooner, more server load. Higher = ignores them longer, lighter server.", "5584b9c9", 24 },
    { "How often each dog decides what to do (fight, guard, hunt). Lower = reacts faster, more server load. Higher = reacts slower, lighter server. Counted in server ticks, not seconds: a healthy server runs about 16 ticks a second, a full one can drop under 5, so 60 here means anywhere from 4 to 13 seconds.", "441022cf", 24 },
    { "Hunt diag", "6f034f1a", 24 },
    { "Hunting: ?", "3de8ad9e", 24 },
    { "Idle dog report interval (ms)", "805bbc52", 24 },
    { "Idle dogs walk around and interact. Cosmetic only, costs a little performance.", "b2841207", 24 },
    { "Idle dogs wander: ?", "ee5da9c3", 24 },
    { "Live perf readout and the tick/region/sniff budgets, applied server-side.", "f5a9c36a", 24 },
    { "Mature pup", "a121a97b", 24 },
    { "Max checks a resting dog skips. Lower = reacts faster, more server load. Higher = reacts slower, lighter server. 0 = never rests.", "1f342ab9", 24 },
    { "Max checks skipped when quiet", "723684b1", 24 },
    { "Max dogs per stream packet", "b3372cf6", 24 },
    { "Measurement: ?", "f7af7313", 24 },
    { "Moving dog report interval (ms)", "6f60c3ca", 24 },
    { "Moving dog sync (ms)", "2e866f52", 24 },
    { "MP only. A dog that no other player can see reports this many times slower than the two intervals above. Lower = more packets, no visible change. Higher = fewer packets. 1 = off. On a full server most dogs are unseen most of the time, so this is the cheapest saving in the list.", "1634fa0e", 24 },
    { "MP only. How close the owner must be for their game to control the dog. Lower = server does more of the work, more server load. Higher = owner's game takes over sooner, smoother. Keep it below 30.", "6de26b77", 24 },
    { "MP only. How far away a player can be and still receive a following dog's smoothed position, a little shorter on diagonals. Lower = far fewer packets on a busy server, distant dogs move in steps. Higher = smooth further out, but the work grows with the area, so doubling this is closer to four times the cost. It also decides when a dog counts as seen by nobody, which is what triggers the slowdown further down this list.", "a16bdb7b", 24 },
    { "MP only. How many dogs fit in one position update. Lower = smaller packets, extra dogs in a crowd move in steps. Higher = everyone stays smooth in a crowd, bigger packets. Only matters where many dogs gather in one place.", "fdcc7fd7", 24 },
    { "MP only. How often players near a following dog receive its smoothed position. Lower = smoother for them, more packets. Higher = fewer packets, slightly choppier for them. Never fires faster than one server tick.", "5abaccd8", 24 },
    { "MP only. How often the owner's game reports a dog standing still. Lower = more packets. Higher = fewer packets, no visible change.", "d40b643c", 24 },
    { "MP only. How often the owner's game reports a dog that is moving. Lower = more packets, the server's copy keeps up better. Higher = fewer packets, the server's copy trails further behind and other players see the older position. This is the busy half of the pair with the idle interval below. Never fires faster than one server tick.", "36cf2512", 24 },
    { "MP only. Position update rate for dogs following or fighting, sent to every player. Lower = smoother, more packets. Higher = fewer packets, choppier for players standing near someone else's dog. Never fires faster than one server tick.", "f811e538", 24 },
    { "MP only. Slowest an unseen dog will report, whatever the slowdown above works out to. Lower = more packets. Higher = fewer packets, but the server's copy can drift further before another player walks up and sees the dog.", "85a63707", 24 },
    { "ON: dogs can hunt.\n \nOFF: hunting is off for everyone on the server.\nDogs ignore prey even with Hunt mode on, and the\nforaging bonus and the foraging scout stop working.", "f182f8c9", 24 },
    { "ON: the owner's game moves the dog, the server only checks it.\nSmooth movement, more network packets.\n \nOFF: the server moves every dog.\nFewer packets, choppy movement, more server load.", "fc8deaed", 24 },
    { "Only the disk part of the command above. For re-running the sweep without touching the dogs currently in the world.", "4366468f", 24 },
    { "Quick 'is there a building here?' checks that count as one full scan. Lower = slower spawning, lighter server. Higher = faster spawning, more server load. 1 = off.", "7e9ce327", 24 },
    { "Quick checks per full scan", "21fb02ce", 24 },
    { "Reads before an area is marked as having no place for strays. Lower = lighter server, strays may feel rare. Higher = more strays, more server load. 1 = old behaviour.", "08243f42", 24 },
    { "Reads before marking an area done", "69805148", 24 },
    { "Restore defaults", "9fa0d187", 24 },
    { "Scans allowed in the same tick. Lower = smaller stutters, slower spawning. Higher = bigger stutters, faster spawning. Adjust the rate above first.", "aa031a7b", 24 },
    { "Search size for reachable zombies. Lower = lighter server, but below 625 dogs may chase zombies they cannot reach. Higher = safer, more server load.", "4c9c3dc7", 24 },
    { "Self time: each ms counts in one row only, so the rows add up.", "a14908f9", 24 },
