    { "A deal you hear is real: it applies to every player for 24 in-game hours.", "9428b075", 111 },
    { "Any two-way radio with power works: a walkie-talkie in your hand or on your belt, or a ham radio or base station placed in the world. Walkies need a working battery and must be switched on.", "ef9406ff", 111 },
    { "Buy tab: what the trader has right now. Stock is a fresh random draw every restock, every 24 hours by default.", "9b753fc0", 111 },
    { "Contraband Items only appear while Trade: Contraband is on. Turning Contraband off also stops Late Night.", "5c96640f", 111 },
    { "Dead drops: orders aren't handed over on the spot. When your package is ready, right-click any mailbox and pick Collect package.", "a41674aa", 111 },
    { "Example for Custom Items (Sell): sparks:Base.Battery:5:10. Custom Items (Buy) uses the same format; the last number is how many they'll buy.", "08bc1655", 111 },
    { "Ironside lends money: pay it back before the deadline. Wrench sells used cars: follow the green arrow to find yours.", "8ed3f3e5", 111 },
    { "Item lines use this format: trader:Module.Item:price:qty, separated by semicolons. Traders: sparks, doc, ironside, owl, wrench, ranger, homestead.", "bbac3994", 111 },
    { "Items you're wearing, holding or have marked as favorite are never sold. The exception is generators: carry one in your hands to sell it to Sparks. A generator placed on the ground has to be picked up first.", "009d9778", 111 },
    { "Jobs tab: contracts and story jobs. Services: Wrench refills gas cans, car batteries and propane, and Sparks repairs generators.", "a1894625", 111 },
    { "Make an offer to haggle on a price. Push too hard and they hang up on you.", "2e05d87c", 111 },
    { "Never paste quote marks into these text settings. A stray \" can break the saved settings file and blank your lines.", "d02498d6", 111 },
    { "Only Sell Custom Items: trader shelves show only your custom items and items added by other mods. Buying, events and rushes keep working.", "6012ae9b", 111 },
    { "Optional add-ons ship with the mod: tick Radio Traders x Guns of 93 or Radio Traders x Drugs of 93 in the mod list.", "62843279", 111 },
    { "Price Overrides use Item=Price. Item Blacklist takes item IDs separated by semicolons. The Trader switches take a trader off the air entirely.", "00914fff", 111 },
    { "RADIO TRADERS", "aeeb8d89", 111 },
    { "Ranger always buys jewelry, gems and precious metals. A gold, silver or gem rush on the radio means she pays extra until the next day.", "a468683b", 111 },
    { "Rare events can happen when a trader answers: Doc's House Call, Ranger's Open Season, Night Owl's Chef's Table and Late Night, and Ironside's Mayhem.", "a36e3dc8", 111 },
    { "Reputation: five standings per trader, from Distrusted to Partner. Yours shows as REP in the call window. Better standing means better prices.", "20863c2e", 111 },
    { "Right-click the radio and pick Radio Traders, or use the button in the radio's own window.", "63ca241c", 111 },
    { "Secret stock: pay for a peek at a few extra items. It costs more each time you ask in the same call.", "2e646579", 111 },
    { "Sell tab: what the trader will buy. What you get depends on the item's condition, charge left, or how much food is left.", "66241fee", 111 },
    { "Short on cash? With PZLinux and a Credit Card in your inventory, traders can charge your bank instead, if the server allows it.", "370ac453", 111 },
    { "These features depend on the server's settings, so some may be switched off.", "42ae5666", 111 },
    { "Traders announce deals on their own radio frequency. It's shown in your radio's window and on the welcome bulletin. Tune any radio there to listen.", "c3e64a97", 111 },
    { "Traders keep their own hours and don't always answer. Night Owl only picks up after dark. Better radios and clear weather help; a weak signal garbles the line and can drop the call.", "b30e273e", 111 },
    { "Wrong trader answered, or yours is off the air? Pay whoever is on the line to relay you to someone else.", "d9fe226d", 111 },
    { "No way, I know where it is", "f79c2842", 112 },
